11. Apply PHATE using its defaultsThe familiar fit_transform pattern now receives text-derived features. We fix only the random seed and leave the other settings at their defaults.There are two different representations here: each model embedding has hundreds of features; each PHATE point has two plotting coordinates. PHATE axes do not have topic names, and a visible gap does not by itself establish separate groups. Use the map to choose texts to inspect.

import phatereducer = phate.PHATE(random_state=386)coordinates = reducer.fit_transform(X)print("Plotted coordinate matrix:", coordinates.shape)


df["PHATE1"] = coordinates[:, 0]df["PHATE2"] = coordinates[:, 1]df[["title", "PHATE1", "PHATE2"]].head()
